Just a little smear there.

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:54.270
Now, let's, what is this?

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:56.370
Uncle Bob.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:57.250
Yeah, yes, Chuck.

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:59.680
Uncle Bob, how are you picked for money?

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.220
Oh, fine, thanks. I don't need any.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:04.640
Well, there's a dance tonight, and I'm a little short.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.240
Well, dance with a short girl. Nobody will notice it.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:10.300
Uncle Bob, what I mean is...

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:13.260
Just look, if you want something, just come right out and ask for it.

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.820
I don't like people who beat around the bush.

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:18.060
Uncle Bob, can I have ten bucks?

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:19.790
No, but I like you better now.

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:25.220
Hold it, sister.

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:27.440
Look, I've got to warn Mr. Collins. Steve's on his way.

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:28.100
Who's Steve?

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:29.160
Oh, never mind. Stop me.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:29.700
Bob!

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:40.320
You're back! I can't!

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:46.760
Now!

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:47.920
Ow!

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:51.660
Diner!

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.760
Shulti, I just can't tell you.

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:06.590
You can't make me win.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:15.190
It's so terrible to tell you.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:16.210
You better sit down.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:17.610
Oh, no, no, not right now, Shulti.

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:18.090
I don't have time.

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:18.570
Tell me.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:18.790
Go ahead.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:21.480
Well, I told this gorilla out at the plant

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:22.540
that you were my boyfriend,

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.840
and he's on his way over here to beat you to a pulp.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:25.580
Ah, ah.

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:32.190
and I thought that I'd get rid of him.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:35.010
Shultz, you mean he's really tough?

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.920
Well, he lifts rockets for exercise.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:38.420
Golly.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.420
Would you like me to get rid of him for you, Shultz?

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:43.560
He's a monster.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:44.460
Answer my question.

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:45.140
Well, yeah, how?

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:48.140
You've heard of psychological warfare, Shultz.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:48.400
Yeah.

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:51.810
You're going to see it in operation right now.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:53.320
Chuck Boy?

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:54.260
Yeah, Bob?

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:56.000
Would you bring that prop door over here, please?

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:58.480
And fellas, Mildred, I got an extra job for you.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:19:59.460
Sit down, Shultz.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:15.990
Well, he's in there, but please don't go in.

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:17.040
Bandits.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.260
See, I'm begging you.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:19.600
Your blood will be on my hands.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:23.680
That's whose blood?

00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:24.750
Yours.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.260
You know who he is, don't you?

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:29.720
Yeah, Bob Collins.

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:32.220
Well, his professional name is Killer Collins.

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:34.520
Killer Collins?

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:36.100
Yeah, well, certainly you've heard of...

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:37.240
Oh, no, that's right.

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:39.460
You're from the East, and he was Pacific Coast champion.

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:40.720
Of what?

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:41.500
Boxing.

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:45.680
Who are you kidding?

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:49.870
Hey, where is he?

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:53.210
Take it this is the foolhardy young man?

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:53.960
I'm afraid so.

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:54.970
Who are you?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.960
I'm Mr. Darrow, the attorney for the building.

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.840
Would you sign these papers for me, please?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.580
Sign what?

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:02.570
Well, it's nothing really.

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:06.050
It's just a release absolving the owners of the building and Mr. Collins

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:08.600
from all legal and financial responsibilities

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:12.330
in connection with your hospitalization.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:15.320
I ain't going to no hospital.

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:18.010
Well, don't you think we ought to let the doctor make that decision

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:20.930
after the killer, Mr. Collins, has finished with you?

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.210
I'll go tell the doctor we're ready for it.

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:23.700
Thank you.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.040
Now, just sign right here, sir.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.990
I ain't signing nothing.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:29.800
Look, that's a felony.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.640
for a prizefighter to strike an ordinary man.

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.300
Now, it would be much different if he were fighting

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:36.800
men like these again.

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:41.770
Hey, did Collins fight these guys?

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:43.840
Read the inscriptions if you like.

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:48.120
Baby, you're the top's Maxie Rosenblum.

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:55.270
To the greatest Max Baird.

00:21:56.470 --> 00:21:57.150
Now, what'd you say?

00:21:58.220 --> 00:21:58.960
That's him, Doctor.

00:21:59.260 --> 00:21:59.680
Oh, yes.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.220
Hey, what is this?

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:01.820
Quiet, please.

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:02.920
He's the doctor for the building.

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:04.180
But I don't want to get a...

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:05.860
Exhale.

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:08.360
Oh, this man's in great shape.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:09.260
He'll take a tremendous beating.

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:10.390
Oh, please.

00:22:11.940 --> 00:22:14.580
It's much too nice looking to have your face all mashed in

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:15.680
and your bones broken.

00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:22.040
Yes, I would only lay off those kidney punches.

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:24.650
It keeps him in the hospital so long.

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:42.630
the killer wants to know if that sucker's here yet you him well hey chad he's here now nurse

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:47.290
hawkins you're overstepping your bounds unlock that door doctor please i don't mind accidents

00:22:47.290 --> 00:22:53.310
or operations or anything like that but to see this nice looking young man all mangled and bleeding

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:16.950
Yeah, he'll sign it when he comes, too.

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:23.250
Don't you dare hit me. It's a felony.

00:23:24.180 --> 00:23:26.670
You can go to jail. You see, I'm only a kid.

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:28.830
Give him a break, killer. I know he won't bother me anymore.

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:29.770
Listen, killer.

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:31.260
I don't even know her.

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:37.020
I came in here by accident.

00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:40.110
I'm on my way back east.

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:50.360
Let me out of here.

00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:53.280
Whatever.

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.060
I guess we might as well get the picture.

00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:11.320
We'll have to bring the killer, too, first.

00:24:34.600 --> 00:24:46.590
Played by Barbara Nichols, Steve by Steve Marlow, Frank by Michael Rode, Mildred by Kathleen Hughes, Mr. Williams by Jack Holland, and Bill by yours truly, Bill Baldwin.
